  "family": "Magnoliaceae",
  "memo": "&lt;em&gt;Magnolia grandiflora 'Majestic Beauty'&lt;/em&gt; is a cultivar of the Southern magnolia, distinguished by its large size, pyramidal form, and open canopy. The leaves are substantial, with a glossy deep green upper surface and a bronze-toned underside. The flowers consist of fleshy white tepals surrounding stamens on a central receptacle. After pollination, the tree develops distinctive seed cones that release seeds encased in a waxy red coat. Magnolia borers can be a problematic pest, and these cultivars are also prone to girdling.",
